      "designInstructions": "# Lab-Grade Technical Design Language\n\nThis design system communicates institutional authority and technical precision through a \"Lab Grade\" aesthetic. It prioritizes information density and deterministic clarity over marketing ornamentation.\n\n### Layout Signatures\n- **Hairline Grids**: Define section boundaries and feature lists using strict 1px rules instead of shadows or colored backgrounds. Use a 4-column matrix for technical specifications.\n- **Horizontal Infrastructure Chains**: Visualize data flow (ERP -> MLV -> Production) using rigid horizontal chains with thin arrows.\n- **Terminal Readouts**: Use dark-mode terminal windows with standard window chrome to showcase API responses and technical implementation details.\n\n### Border & Shape Eccentricities\n- **Sharp Radii**: Every element uses a strict 0px corner radius (rounded-none). No rounded pills or cards.\n- **Hairline Boundaries**: Components are delineated by hairline borders (#E5E7EB) to maintain a sterile, high-ink-ratio feel.\n\n### Decorative Motifs\n- **Active Scan-Lines**: Incorporate vertical or horizontal sweeping scan-lines in (--k-color-accent) over imagery to simulate live verification.\n- **Metric HUDs**: Overlay technical metadata (FPS, Latency, Buffer IDs) in small, monospaced text around functional widgets.\n\n### Spacing & Density Rhythm\n- **Institutional Density**: High information density within components, balanced by generous section-level padding (py-32).\n- **Tabular Data**: Use editorial spec-sheet layouts (capability ledgers) where feature name, description, and metric are weighted equally on a single row.\n\n### Micro-Details\n- **Status Indicators**: Use small circular pips with a pulse effect for \"Live\" status.\n- **Technical Tags**: Use small, high-contrast badges with subtle background tints (#20B2AA at 0.1 opacity) for valid/invalid states.\n- **Typography**: Encode Sans for commanding headings; Space Grotesk for body and technical data readouts.",
      "created": "2026-06-13T08:31:16.419134+00:00",
      "modified": "2026-06-13T08:31:16.419134+00:00"
    },
